zsh/.zshenv and zsh/ghostty-integration are Ghostty's zsh shell integration,
copied unmodified from vendor/gpui-libghostty/crates/gpui-ghostty/vendor/ghostty
(src/shell-integration/zsh). They started as a copy of Kitty's zsh integration
and are distributed under the GNU General Public License version 3; see COPYING
and the license header at the top of each file.

bareframe runs zsh with ZDOTDIR pointing at the zsh directory. The .zshenv there
restores the user's ZDOTDIR, sources the user's own startup files and installs
hooks that report the working directory (OSC 7) and set the terminal title.
